        "username": "drstein",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/cab0a1/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-24T22:11:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Christopher&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Christopher\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah, I did see that, and it’s a fair point.  Unfortunately, at this point, we couldn’t include something like that in the Enhanced Edition box.  However, that doesn’t mean something like that couldn’t happen - we’re just too late to make it part of the official core game re-release.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That was the idea of my request. Had we been able to try the tokens before the enhanced edition is prepared, we would have been capable of sending feedback and our ideas. Well, for third edition, I guess.</p>\n<p>By the way, what are tokens going to be? I guess the round ones are hit points…but what about rectangular ones? only those that are in the last figure? or will we have things like “end of turn effect”, “X damage to highest hp hero at the end of turn”, etc…?</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:03:34.624Z",
